        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0244" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg210"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 311.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 307, of the
                    29th ultimo, I have the honor to transmit herewith, a copy and translation of a
                    note which has just been received from the German foreign office, in reply to my
                    note of that date, in regard to the treatment of naturalized American citizens
                    of German origin upon their return to their native country, and to be, sir,
                    etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d196-a1.xml" xpointer="d196-a1"/>
